# ==========================================================================
# BLOOM'S MODEL CARDS -- its own, one per gun.
#
# EVERY SET IS ITS OWN SET OF CARDS (the owner, 2026-09-20). Bloom had none: its ten guns
# named `model = BL_*` and rode Blood's cards outright, which meant they rode Blood's PROPS,
# which meant they rode BLOOD'S PLACEMENT CVARS. Tune Bloom's Tesla Rifle and you moved
# Blood's. Bloom had no slider page of its own because it had nothing of its own to point at.
#
# `base = <card>` IS THE RIG'S OWN MECHANISM (RS_VR_Reload parser.zs, key `base`): the card
# is built from a FRESH COPY of the named one with these lines laid over it. So Bloom gets a
# real card per gun -- its own id, its own prop, its own ten cvars, its own sliders -- while
# NOT ONE MEASURED NUMBER IS COPIED OR RETYPED HERE. The meshes are the same objects; the
# measurements stay where they were measured, on Blood's cards, and stay in one place.
#
# GENERATED. Change the sheet and run _pending/tools/make_bloom_cards.py again.
# ==========================================================================

weapon "BM_Pitchfork"
  base       = BL_Pitchfork
  prop       = "BM_PropPitchfork"
end

